{"chunk":"For the purposes of this article only, the following words and phrases, when capitalized,\n               shall have the meanings indicated. Accessible or Accessible to Physically Disabled Persons shall be as defined in Chapter 521 of the Code of Massachusetts Regulations, as amended. Applicant shall mean any person or entity having a legal or equitable interest in a Proposed\n                  Project subject, in accordance with Section 30-3, to the provisions of this article, or the authorized agent of any such person or\n                  entity. Hotel Use shall mean Use Item Number 15, as defined in Table B of Section 8-3 (Use Regulations). Physically Disabled Person shall be as defined in Chapter 521 of the Code of Massachusetts Regulations, as amended. Proposed Project shall mean the erection or extension of any structure or part thereof, or the change\n                  of use of any structure or land, for which the Applicant is required to obtain a building\n                  or use permit. Residential Use shall mean Use Item Numbers 7, 7A, 7B, 8, 8A, 10, 11, 12, 13, 13A, or 14, as defined\n                  in Table B, Section 8-3 (Use Regulations). Zoning Relief shall mean any zoning variance, exception, conditional use permit, or zoning map\n                  or text change, or any other relief granted by the Zoning Commission or the Board\n                  of Appeal. (Text Amd.","document":"ARTICLE_30_-_BARRIER-FREE_ACCESS","city":"boston","heading_1":"ARTICLE 30 BARRIER-FREE ACCESS","heading_2":"Section 30-2. Definitions.","url":"https:\/\/library.municode.com\/MA\/Boston\/codes\/Redevelopment_Authority?nodeId=ART30BAEEAC_S30-2DE","district_code":[],"district_category":[],"embedding":[-0.0127956672,-0.017966941,-0.0012702475,-0.02122402,0.0043020905,0.0297931489,0.0569844954,-0.0266671106,0.0186507721,0.056609761,0.0335783847,0.0239125025,0.0581530556,-0.022784913,0.0316970162,-0.0172779392,0.0015313885,0.0145108998,-0.0192035194,-0.076761469